When a player (other than me) is leaving the world, the VRCPlayerApi.GetPlayers(players) seems to return invalid objects.

My code:

// World capacity is 6, so create a new array with length of 12 (Hard cap)
private VRCPlayerApi[] players = new VRCPlayerApi[12];

void Update() {
  VRCPlayerApi.GetPlayers(players);
    for (int i = 0; i < players.Length; i++) {
      if (players[i] == null) 
        continue;
      Vector3 position = players[i].GetPosition(); <--- CRASH
}

I use UdonSharp, but maybe it's a general problem in the API.
